RAPH","id":"do409","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"   The weather outside is turning colder here again so I've been looking for a little something spicy to warm up with. Something that's not too heavy. This lean round steak beef curry is just the thing!","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7ikoc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4g8lj","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"It's super simple because I'm cheating and using a prepared madras spice blend instead of my own. It takes a while because it needs to simmer on the stove for about 1 1/2 hours to make the beef juicy and fall apart tender but all it takes is three easy 10 minute cooking segments to make this beautiful pot of warm spicy yum! ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bjnih","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3407f","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Don't we all have other things we can do while the waiting for the pot to simmer? Usually I'm doing laundry and setting the table but you could be reading a great book, catching up with a friend on the phone, playing games with the kids or even entertaining dinner guests. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cdfo4","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"tti","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"eo64t","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"2h1ju","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_e509fe71db804dfcbfb7b888914bc76a~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Beef Curry Stir-fry"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"abmr1","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" I start out by stir-frying the thinly sliced pieces of round steak in batches. This takes about 5 minutes.  I usually do 2-3 batches for about 1 1-2 pounds of steak. It's best to do this at a high heat to sear the outside quickly. Don't let the meat boil in too much liquid. This will happen of the pieces of meat are crowded in your pan and the temperature is too low.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"96tci","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"GALLERY","id":"sfbv","nodes":[],"galleryData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"items":[{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_a42efefd99a642aa9c0b7cc455326da5~mv2.jpg"},"width":918,"height":802}},"title":"Stir-fry the beef"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_9202d32bd2bd4a3f85fb3ab583253290~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1000}},"title":"Prepare stock and curry"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_f395c624186b495eabe26b4d6a69555c~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1125}},"title":"Saute the onions"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_cd0a4f93ecf64416a20bd4bac68661d4~mv2.jp